\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.1}{\ignorespaces Multiwavelength composite of the Coma cluster (Abell 1656). Top left: Planck tSZ Compton $y$ map. Top right: ROSAT soft X-ray surface brightness. In both upper panels the X-ray contours are superimposed on the tSZ image to illustrate the complementary spatial coverage of the two windows. Bottom panels show each overlaid on the Digitised Sky Survey optical image, revealing the member galaxy distribution. Image credit: ESA/LFI \& HFI Consortia; Max-Planck-Institut f\"{u}r extraterrestrische Physik; NASA, ESA, and the Digitised Sky Survey 2 \textcolor {red}{[ref]} \textcolor {red}{[ref]}.}}{5}{figure.1.1}\protected@file@percent }
